<title>HONG KONG: New World PCS mandates HK$1.5 bln loan.</title>
<headline>New World PCS mandates HK$1.5 bln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New World PCS Ltd has mandated Deutsche Bank Hong Kong to arrange a HK$1.5 billion loan facility, bankers said.</p>
<p>New World Development Co will guarantee 85 percent of the deal, and Total Access Communications Plc will guarantee the remaining 15 percent, they said.</p>
<p>The facility has a effective tenor of five years.</p>
<p>Pricing details are not yet available.</p>
<p>An underwriting group is being formed.</p>
<p>Proceeds are to be used for the company's development of Personal Communication System.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
